[00:38:07.540 --> 00:38:12.540]   - Joseph Graves, we will talk about this when we get home.
[00:38:14.820 --> 00:38:16.780]   - Well, this is yours.
[00:38:16.780 --> 00:38:17.620]   - Thank you.
[00:38:23.100 --> 00:38:24.100]   - Good morning.
[00:38:24.100 --> 00:38:25.460]   They're late for school.
[00:38:25.460 --> 00:38:26.420]   - No way late.
[00:38:26.420 --> 00:38:27.460]   - Hey, I got a bow.
[00:38:27.460 --> 00:38:28.300]   - Hey, I'll take it.
[00:38:28.300 --> 00:38:29.620]   - Long's takin' us.
[00:38:29.620 --> 00:38:31.500]   - Anne Ball, you have two seconds to say hello to your father.
[00:38:31.500 --> 00:38:32.940]   - Hello to my father.
[00:38:32.940 --> 00:38:34.420]   - Oh, no.
[00:38:34.420 --> 00:38:36.140]   - Okay, time's up.
[00:38:36.140 --> 00:38:36.980]   Let's go.
[00:38:38.780 --> 00:38:39.700]   Done.
[00:38:39.700 --> 00:38:40.740]   - Yes, darling.
[00:38:40.740 --> 00:38:42.340]   - You smell really bad.
[00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:46.940]   - I love you guys.
[00:38:50.980 --> 00:38:51.820]   - Graves.
[00:38:52.980 --> 00:38:54.540]   - Captain Pearson had a few questions
[00:38:54.540 --> 00:38:56.540]   about how things were handled,
[00:38:56.540 --> 00:38:59.220]   and recommended that you take a few weeks off.
[00:38:59.220 --> 00:39:01.020]   But I said no.
[00:39:01.020 --> 00:39:02.020]   - Thank you, sir.
[00:39:04.140 --> 00:39:06.020]   - Can I trust you to keep it together?
[00:39:07.460 --> 00:39:09.740]   Look me in the eye and tell me I can trust you.
[00:39:11.980 --> 00:39:13.300]   You can trust me.
[00:39:13.300 --> 00:39:14.140]   - Good.
[00:39:15.340 --> 00:39:16.860]   Your team supports you, and so do I.
[00:39:16.860 --> 00:39:17.700]   - Thank you, sir.
[00:39:23.820 --> 00:39:26.060]   (squeaking)
[00:39:29.180 --> 00:39:30.020]   - You?
[00:39:30.020 --> 00:39:31.980]   Swell's comin' in, I got next to porn.
[00:39:33.820 --> 00:39:34.660]   - Dharma?
[00:39:37.580 --> 00:39:38.420]   Dharma?
[00:39:42.940 --> 00:39:44.660]   Dharma, you can't sleep through the day.
[00:39:52.980 --> 00:39:55.740]   (dramatic music)
[00:40:01.740 --> 00:40:02.900]   - I'm sorry.
[00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:04.860]   I can't be alone right now.
[00:40:06.860 --> 00:40:09.620]   (dramatic music)
[00:40:09.620 --> 00:40:10.620]   - Okay.
[00:40:10.620 --> 00:40:12.620]   - Ralph, may you hold me?
[00:40:14.620 --> 00:40:16.700]   - Do you have to do, I can't be pleased.
[00:40:16.700 --> 00:40:19.460]   (dramatic music)
[00:40:22.300 --> 00:40:25.060]   (dramatic music)
[00:40:31.460 --> 00:40:33.940]   - Why don't you go ahead and show the video?
[00:40:33.940 --> 00:40:35.540]   - My name is Richard Taggart,
[00:40:37.620 --> 00:40:38.940]   and I'm the face of America.
[00:40:40.540 --> 00:40:43.180]   Everything that I'm about to tell you comes from my heart.
[00:40:45.220 --> 00:40:47.300]   For 17 years, I was a soldier.
[00:40:48.460 --> 00:40:52.060]   On SEAL Team Six, the most elite,
[00:40:52.060 --> 00:40:54.140]   special operations team in the world.
[00:40:55.780 --> 00:41:00.420]   On September 3rd, in Canara, Afghanistan, 2014,
[00:41:01.540 --> 00:41:04.060]   I murdered an unarmed American
[00:41:05.100 --> 00:41:07.180]   who had surrendered peacefully.
[00:41:11.900 --> 00:41:16.100]   I know now, excuse me, this is very hard for me to admit
[00:41:18.580 --> 00:41:22.260]   that I was nothing more than a hired assassin
[00:41:23.700 --> 00:41:25.020]   committed war crimes.
[00:41:28.900 --> 00:41:30.980]   To the rest of the world,
[00:41:30.980 --> 00:41:33.460]   rise up and fight America's endless war
[00:41:33.460 --> 00:41:35.020]   against innocent Muslims.
[00:41:36.740 --> 00:41:40.540]   To America, take back your own soul,
[00:41:41.940 --> 00:41:43.980]   your dream of justice and freedom.
[00:41:45.940 --> 00:41:47.900]   To my brothers on SEAL Team Six,
[00:41:49.020 --> 00:41:51.020]   (sighs)
[00:41:51.020 --> 00:41:52.420]   look inside your hearts,
[00:41:56.060 --> 00:41:59.460]   let your better nature of the truth
[00:42:01.220 --> 00:42:02.300]   that it's shined through.
[00:42:05.180 --> 00:42:08.540]   It's not too late, I am proof of that.
